# Planning and Scope Control

For substantial changes, produce a plan before editing:
- User problem and desired outcome.
- Confirmed current behavior.
- Acceptance criteria and edge cases.
- Proposed approach and alternatives where consequential.
- Files/modules likely to change and why.
- Data/API/interface impact.
- Risks, migration needs and rollback considerations.
- Test plan and verification commands.
- Explicit out-of-scope items.

Do not begin implementation until the user approves the plan when the task is substantial, ambiguous, high-risk or explicitly asks for planning first. Keep tiny, obvious fixes lightweight.
